From 186dfa1b40569b7d7bfe1661715820280b35ea37 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aria2-Pro-Core <builder@local>
Date: Sat, 23 May 2026 15:06:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] rpc: add removeFiles flag plus rpc-remove-files-default
 option
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds optional boolean parameter (index 1) to aria2.remove,
aria2.forceRemove and aria2.removeDownloadResult. When true, downloaded
files and their .aria2 control file are deleted along with the task or
result. When omitted, the new --rpc-remove-files-default option decides
(default false, matching upstream behavior). Explicit removeFiles=false
always keeps files, so existing clients are unaffected.

For trailing optional parameters a local checkOptionalParam<T> helper
treats a wrong-type slot as 'not present' instead of throwing — upstream
RPC silently ignores unknown trailing params, and clients that send
extras of unexpected types for slot 1 must keep working.
